# Schema: Polkadot SDK PRDoc Schema (prdoc) v1.0.0
# See doc at https://raw.githubusercontent.com/paritytech/polkadot-sdk/master/prdoc/schema_user.json

title: "Remove libsecp256k1, enforce low-S ECDSA signatures (BIP-62 / EIP-2)"

doc:
  - audience: Runtime Dev
    description: |
      Completes the claims pallet migration from the deprecated `libsecp256k1` crate to
      `secp256k1` and introduces low-S signature normalization (BIP-62 / EIP-2) across
      pallet-revive EVM transaction validation and BEEFY ECDSA signature verification.

      **Claims pallet** — `libsecp256k1` is removed from `polkadot-runtime-common` dependencies
      and all feature flags. The test/benchmark helper `secp_utils::eth()` is corrected to use
      `serialize_uncompressed()` (the `secp256k1` crate's `serialize()` returns 33 compressed
      bytes, not the 65 uncompressed bytes expected by the caller).

      **sp_core::ecdsa** — A new public constant `SECP256K1_HALF_ORDER` and helper function
      `is_signature_normalized()` are added, providing a reusable check for whether a 65-byte
      ECDSA signature has its S value in the lower half of the secp256k1 curve order.
      `Pair::sign_prehashed()` now includes a debug assertion that produced signatures are low-S,
      and the `k256` (no_std) path performs explicit normalization.

      **pallet-revive** — `recover_eth_address()` now rejects signatures where S > N/2 before
      calling `secp256k1_ecdsa_recover`, matching Ethereum post-Homestead transaction validation
      (EIP-2). The `ECRecover` precompile is intentionally unchanged to match Ethereum behavior.

      **sp-consensus-beefy** — `ecdsa_crypto::BeefyAuthorityId::verify()` now rejects signatures
      where S > N/2 before calling `secp256k1_ecdsa_recover_compressed`. This ensures BEEFY
      signatures are always in the canonical form expected by Ethereum-side light clients.

      **secp256k1 dependency** — Upgraded from 0.30.0 to 0.31.1. Call sites are adapted to the
      0.31 API: signing/recovery methods now take `Into<Message>` instead of `&Message`, and
      `SecretKey::from_byte_array` takes an owned array instead of a reference.

      Host functions (`secp256k1_ecdsa_recover`, `ecdsa_verify`, etc.) and
      `Pair::verify()`/`Pair::verify_prehashed()` are not changed to preserve backward
      compatibility with historical block verification.

  - audience: Runtime User
    description: |
      EVM transactions submitted to pallet-revive now require low-S signatures per EIP-2. All
      standard Ethereum signing libraries already produce low-S signatures by default, so no
      action is needed for well-behaved signers. Transactions with non-canonical (high-S)
      signatures will be rejected at validation time.

      BEEFY ECDSA signature verification now also requires low-S. Validators using standard
      signing tooling are unaffected.

crates:
  - name: polkadot-runtime-common
    bump: patch
  - name: sp-core
    bump: minor
  - name: sp-io
    bump: patch
  - name: pallet-revive
    bump: patch
  - name: sp-consensus-beefy
    bump: patch
